    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d316">

                <pb facs="0266" n="192" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg192"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Sir F.
                        Brucé</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-09-19"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 19, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to inform you that I have
                    been officially apprised that the Canadian authorities have paid to the banks at
                    St. Albans, in the State of Vermont, thirty-nine thousand five<hi
                        rendition="#small-caps"/> hundred and twelve dollars and seventy-five cents
                    in gold, and thirty thousand and ten dollars in bank notes, in compliance with
                    an act of the Canadian parliament, on account of the amount deposited with the
                    authorities of that province upon the arrest of the St. Albans marauders.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with the highest consideration, sir, your obedient
                    servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir Frederick W. A. Bruce,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
